1
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:09,290
A sign in a lift says: maximum 8 people.

2
00:00:09,340 --> 00:00:11,650
Can exactly 8 people use the lift?

3
00:00:11,700 --> 00:00:17,280
Think about how you would write the rule with p for the number of people.

4
00:00:17,330 --> 00:00:20,180
Which inequality means maximum 8 people?

5
00:00:20,230 --> 00:00:23,550
Pause the video and choose.

6
00:00:23,600 --> 00:00:26,690
Maximum 8 means 8 is allowed, but 9 is not.

7
00:00:26,740 --> 00:00:29,580
So p is less than or equal to 8.

8
00:00:29,630 --> 00:00:37,360
A ride at a fair says: riders must be at least 140 centimetres, and under 195 centimetres.

9
00:00:37,410 --> 00:00:39,350
Is exactly 140 allowed?

10
00:00:39,400 --> 00:00:41,190
Is exactly 195?

11
00:00:41,240 --> 00:00:47,120
Remember: x is greater than 3 means x is more than 3, but 3 itself is not included.

12
00:00:47,170 --> 00:00:50,890
On a number line, it has an open circle at 3.

13
00:00:50,940 --> 00:00:53,450
This sign means less than or equal to.

14
00:00:53,500 --> 00:00:56,150
This one means greater than or equal to.

15
00:00:56,200 --> 00:01:00,810
The boundary is included, so we draw a closed, filled circle.

16
00:01:00,860 --> 00:01:03,520
Here is x greater than or equal to 2.

17
00:01:03,570 --> 00:01:06,840
The closed circle shows 2 is included.

18
00:01:06,890 --> 00:01:07,540
Your turn.

19
00:01:07,590 --> 00:01:11,650
How is x greater than or equal to 3 shown on a number line?

20
00:01:11,700 --> 00:01:14,920
Pause the video and choose.

21
00:01:14,970 --> 00:01:20,500
3 is included, so it is a closed circle at 3, with an arrow to the right.

22
00:01:20,550 --> 00:01:23,850
Two conditions together make an interval.

23
00:01:23,900 --> 00:01:29,820
The ride rule is: 140 is less than or equal to h, and h is less than 195.

24
00:01:29,870 --> 00:01:33,730
Closed circle at 140, open circle at 195.

25
00:01:33,780 --> 00:01:39,510
This line shows negative 2 is less than or equal to x, which is less than 3.

26
00:01:39,560 --> 00:01:43,930
The integers in it are negative 2, negative 1, 0, 1 and 2.

27
00:01:43,980 --> 00:01:45,850
3 is not included.

28
00:01:45,900 --> 00:01:47,150
Here is the method.

29
00:01:47,200 --> 00:01:54,210
Step 1: decide if each boundary is included, with a closed circle, or not, with an open circle.

30
00:01:54,260 --> 00:02:00,380
Step 2: for an interval, write it in order, with the smallest number on the left.

31
00:02:00,430 --> 00:02:06,140
Step 3: solve an inequality like an equation, doing the same to both sides.

32
00:02:06,190 --> 00:02:11,170
Step 4: when you list integers, check each boundary carefully.

33
00:02:11,220 --> 00:02:17,680
A number line shows an open circle at negative 1, and a closed circle at 4, joined together.

34
00:02:17,730 --> 00:02:19,720
Write the inequality.

35
00:02:19,770 --> 00:02:23,220
Open at negative 1, so negative 1 is less than x.

36
00:02:23,270 --> 00:02:26,980
Closed at 4, so x is less than or equal to 4.

37
00:02:27,030 --> 00:02:27,700
Your turn.

38
00:02:27,750 --> 00:02:31,260
What is the largest integer with x less than 4.5?

39
00:02:31,310 --> 00:02:34,260
Pause and work it out.

40
00:02:34,310 --> 00:02:38,200
The integers less than 4.5 are 4, 3, 2 and so on.

41
00:02:38,250 --> 00:02:40,120
The largest is 4.

42
00:02:40,170 --> 00:02:43,740
Solve 5 x minus 3 is greater than 2 x plus 9.

43
00:02:43,790 --> 00:02:49,130
Subtract 2 x from both sides: 3 x minus 3 is greater than 9.

44
00:02:49,180 --> 00:02:51,590
Add 3: 3 x is greater than 12.

45
00:02:51,640 --> 00:02:54,840
Divide by 3: x is greater than 4.

46
00:02:54,890 --> 00:03:01,490
Find the integers n where 7 is less than or equal to 2 n plus 1, which is less than 15.

47
00:03:01,540 --> 00:03:08,300
Subtract 1 from every part: 6 is less than or equal to 2 n, which is less than 14.

48
00:03:08,350 --> 00:03:14,010
Divide every part by 2: 3 is less than or equal to n, which is less than 7.

49
00:03:14,060 --> 00:03:16,150
So n is 3, 4, 5 or 6.

50
00:03:16,200 --> 00:03:19,720
Mo shows x is at least negative 2 on a number line.

51
00:03:19,770 --> 00:03:21,660
Which line is wrong?

52
00:03:21,710 --> 00:03:22,860
Line 1 is wrong.

53
00:03:22,910 --> 00:03:25,840
At least negative 2 includes negative 2.

54
00:03:25,890 --> 00:03:29,680
So x is greater than or equal to negative 2.

55
00:03:29,730 --> 00:03:33,060
The circle at negative 2 must be closed.

56
00:03:33,110 --> 00:03:35,550
Food safety rules use inequalities.

57
00:03:35,600 --> 00:03:39,610
A fridge should keep food at 5 degrees Celsius or colder.

58
00:03:39,660 --> 00:03:42,580
That is t less than or equal to 5.

59
00:03:42,630 --> 00:03:46,570
A freezer should be at negative 18 degrees or colder.

60
00:03:46,620 --> 00:03:50,430
That is t less than or equal to negative 18.

61
00:03:50,480 --> 00:03:51,760
One last question.

62
00:03:51,810 --> 00:03:55,310
Solve 2 x minus 1 is greater than or equal to 9.

63
00:03:55,360 --> 00:03:58,710
Pause the video and choose.

64
00:03:58,760 --> 00:04:01,880
Add 1: 2 x is greater than or equal to 10.

65
00:04:01,930 --> 00:04:05,830
Divide by 2: x is greater than or equal to 5.

66
00:04:05,880 --> 00:04:11,660
To remember: less than or equal to, and greater than or equal to, include the boundary.

67
00:04:11,710 --> 00:04:13,550
Use a closed circle.

68
00:04:13,600 --> 00:04:16,610
Less than and greater than do not include it.

69
00:04:16,660 --> 00:04:18,450
Use an open circle.

70
00:04:18,500 --> 00:04:22,730
Write intervals with the smallest number on the left.

71
00:04:22,780 --> 00:04:28,270
Solve them like equations, and list integers carefully at each boundary.

72
00:04:28,320 --> 00:04:33,470
Great work! Now practise lesson 2.6 on Camday.
